 definetly a worth souls like title.", "timestamp_created": 1699299720, "timestamp_updated": 1699299720, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.520958065986633301", "comment_count": 2, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "149667506", "author": {"steamid": "76561198059539392", "personaname": "Dizzy Gas", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/DizzyGas/", "num_games_owned": 542, "num_reviews": 43, "playtime_forever": 1058, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 172, "last_played": 1737318009, "avatar": "521375921e391ce071cde9d1a06e2923099356d1"}, "language": "english", "review": "Runs awful, I don't exactly have a top of the line pc, but I've been able to run recent and better looking games way better than this. Hell even Jedi: Survivor ran decently well for me and that was an unoptimized mess, which also looked WAY better than this.\n\nEDIT after upgrading my pc: The game runs fine after upgrading and turning on DLSS and other options that it can't run decently without, however between some of the incredibly frustrating design choices (like getting swarmed by enemies that knock me down, CC me and shoot me from afar) and game-ruining flaws (like the save system somehow failing to save my game on two separate sessions, forcing me to start the game from the very beginning two times in a row, I will never touch this game again. It's ♥♥♥♥", "timestamp_created": 1699299633, "timestamp_updated": 1736693718, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.434782594442367554", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "149660314", "author": {"steamid": "76561199544897282", "personaname": "MrBrownst0n3", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199544897282/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 14, "playtime_forever": 17187, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6928, "last_played": 1729704097, "avatar": "ae540d37eef3cfcff194166b7325340a698fe0e0"}, "language": "english", "review": "Have you ever wanted to throw your mouse and keyboard at your monitor. This is that game. For the first day or two. The it magically becomes like crack. You know the kind in the 90's New Jack City. Bravo to Gunfire Games for taking the franchise and Improving on it in so many ways. From giving us a ton of new archetypes, over 150 rings and amulets. New relics ,a whole bunch of new puzzles and hidden areas. Bang up job guys.", "timestamp_created": 1699290777, "timestamp_updated": 1699290777, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1690300800", "reactions": []}]}